# CPU tier: a host RAM bank for the expert bytes, filled at load by
# sequential reads. The tier read every expert in place from a shared mapping
# of the weight file; when the host-tier experts do not fit in the page cache
# (Flash-Next: 56.4 GiB of expert constants on a 52 GiB host), the misses
# arrive as 128 KiB page-fault reads on the workers (measured: 13-17 % of the
# workers' wall in folio_wait_bit_common; an madvise(WILLNEED) prefetch did
# nothing, a 4 MiB readahead doubled the bytes read).
#
# moe/host_expert_bank.hpp: slots in one anonymous MAP_NORESERVE mapping
# (MOE_CPU_BANK_BYTES; unset = off, the mapping path unchanged). A layer's
# first tier call queues a fill: every expert the static partition does not
# pin to the card, in MOE_CPU_BANK_SEED's per-layer rank (a hot-set seed file,
# `# space=layer_key`), at most MOE_CPU_BANK_FILL_PER_LAYER, each per-tensor
# array read as ONE sequential O_DIRECT range and copied into the slots; the
# fill never evicts. A miss takes a slot (LRU over unpinned slots of its size
# class) and its spans are read with O_DIRECT on MOE_CPU_BANK_IO_THREADS
# (default 8); dispatch_cpu_tier runs the experts already present and the IO
# thread queues a missing expert's compute when its last span lands; the join
# waits for those before the pool. A slot is a hit only for the same spans;
# anything else (no slot, a record being read) reads the mapping as before,
# as does a failed read. The bytes are the file's, so the output is too.
# Ten cells (bytes at unaligned offsets and at the file end, hits, LRU and
# pins, short reads, size classes, the fill's bytes, budget, once-per-layer,
# span mismatch), red on nine mutants.
#
# The fill reads each per-tensor array from its lowest to its highest
# selected expert, card-resident bytes included (59.8 GiB for 56.4 GiB of
# constants); MOE_CPU_BANK_FILL_PER_LAYER bounds the slots, not that read.
# The budget is MAP_NORESERVE: set above the host's free memory it ends in an
# OOM kill. Each layer's fill maps one transient staging range on top.
#
# Served on the B60 (Flash-Next d48s2, ratio 78 + tier + per-expert dispatch,
# 12e9 device slot pool, census112 seed, u8 paged KV, 16 host CPUs, 52 GiB),
# a fresh process, "Hello" then a second prompt, 257 greedy tokens each, text
# byte-identical to the mapping arm on both: decode 48.55 / 34.62 s ->
# 40.42 / 34.11 s at a 40 GiB bank (360 per layer; the budget ran out at 44
# of 48 layers) and 38.18 / 33.77 s, 39.66 / 34.72 s at 46 GiB (370 per
# layer, all 48 layers, ~16,000 experts, ~21 s added to the load). With every
# expert in RAM (the same prompt again in one process) the tier's decode-only
# compute is 1.14 ms per layer call for 7.57 experts, the tier bench's figure.
#
