+// arcint (patch 0072). A host RAM bank for the CPU tier's expert bytes.
+//
+// Before this patch the CPU tier read every expert in place from a shared
+// read-only mapping of the weight file (ParallelWeightReader::mapped). When
+// the host-tier experts do not fit in the page cache (Flash-Next: 56.4 GiB of
+// expert constants against a 44-52 GiB host), each miss arrives as a series
+// of 128 KiB page-fault reads on the worker that touches it: measured on the
+// served decode, the tier's workers spend 13-17 % of the wall in
+// folio_wait_bit_common. An madvise(WILLNEED) prefetch did not help (the
+// kernel caps one call at max(io_pages, ra_pages) = 128 KiB there), and a
+// 4 MiB readahead doubled the bytes read.
+//
+// The bank reads one expert's spans whole, with O_DIRECT, into slots of an
+// anonymous mapping, on its own IO threads, issued when the tier call is
+// dispatched; the caller computes the experts already present first and
+// queues a missing expert's compute when its last span has landed. The bytes
+// are the file's bytes (the same ones the mapping shows), so the tier's
+// output is unchanged. Eviction is LRU over slots not pinned by a running
+// call; a request that finds no free or evictable slot, or whose bytes are
+// being read for another caller, is answered Unbanked and the caller reads
+// the mapping as before.
